      "program_name": "Santa Ana, Anaheim/Orange County Continuum of Care (CA-602) and HHAP",
      "administering_agency": "County of Orange, County Executive Office, Office of Care Coordination (CoC lead agency and HHAP administrative entity); Orange County CoC Board",
      "funding_type": "grant",
      "typical_award_size": "HHAP by round, County of Orange: R1 $7,486,576, R2 $3,422,435, R3 $9,582,817, R4 $7,131,233, R5 $8,346,727, R6 $8,355,062 (agreement through June 30, 2030). Orange County CoC: R1 $8,081,116, R2 $3,823,692, R3 $10,267,304, R4 $7,600,842, R5 $8,699,841, R6 $8,923,350; Anaheim, Santa Ana and Irvine each $5,947,855 in R6 for a regional R6 total of $35,100,000 awarded April 2026. State accountability site: $152,700,000 HHAP rounds 1 to 5 to the Orange County area, $36,000,000 directly to the County ($28,900,000 obligated, $15,300,000 spent by mid-2025); Encampment Resolution Funding $8,700,000 area, $3,600,000 County. HHAP-6 CoC budget: $3,976,421 permanent housing operating subsidies, $592,335 youth operating subsidies, $1,552,663 rapid rehousing, $1,222,663 interim housing operating subsidies, $330,000 youth interim, $624,635 services, $624,635 administration and HMIS. HUD CoC FY 2024 awards to CA-602 included $1,249,326 Permanent Housing Collaborative, $731,787 rapid rehousing and $528,250 Jackson Aisle TRA (partial list). 2024 PIT: 7,322 people, 4,173 unsheltered, 9,751 year-round beds. Homekey+: County RFI (due Nov 27, 2024) qualified Volunteers of America, National CORE, California Supportive Housing, American Family Housing and Weingart Center as development partners.",
      "per_unit_cap": null,
