      "layering_notes": "Huntington Beach's HOME is small ($538,328) and goes almost entirely to TBRA; only the CHDO reserve (about $260,000 a year) is available for development, so City HOME is a token layer next to County and OCHFT money. Davis-Bacon applies at 12 or more HOME-assisted units. The City's Pathways Project (Jamboree Housing ENA extended 18 months in May 2024 for a permanent shelter and supportive housing at the Navigation Center site, Beach and Edinger Corridors Affordable Housing Overlay) was budgeted from IIG, AHSC, TCAC, BHCIP, Community Care Expansion, OCHFT ($2,500,000), OCHA PBVs ($3,720,000) and Behavioral Health Services funds ($5,000,000), illustrating the stack the City expects. Legistar attachments (FY 2025-26 funding tables, 2026-27 NOFA notice, Pathways funding matrix, ENA extension) opened via the Legistar web API; huntingtonbeachca.gov department pages returned 404 at the old paths.",
